.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH access 1  "access " 
.SH NAME
access \- Show who can read/write each folder in one table, and revoke access in place (\-\-revoke)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBaccess\fR [\fB\-\-revoke\fR] [\fB\-\-write\fR] [\fB\-\-read\fR] [\fB\-\-blob\fR] [\fB\-\-full\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show who can read/write each folder in one table, and revoke access in place (\-\-revoke)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-revoke\fR
Revoke a share instead of listing access (requires the positional path or \-\-blob)
.TP
\fB\-\-write\fR
Revoke the write share (default: the read share)
.TP
\fB\-\-read\fR
Revoke the read share (the default, prompt\-free path)
.TP
\fB\-\-blob\fR \fI<BLOB>\fR
Revoke a blob share by content hash (unpins and unannounces the blob) instead of a folder share; requires \-\-revoke
.TP
\fB\-\-full\fR
Show every shared\-with row instead of capping the list
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR]
Folder path or namespace (omit to show every folder)
